---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout
  title="Sierra Leone: DecoPlastic"
  description="DecoPlastic Sierra Leone establishes a locally rooted system for plastic collection, sorting, processing and manufacturing, led by Sierra Leone Engineering Solutions."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal"><a href={base} style="color:inherit;">&larr; Plastic Circle West Africa</a></p>
      <h1 class="reveal">DecoPlastic, Sierra Leone</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal">
        A locally rooted circular economy platform that turns plastic waste
        in Sierra Leone into marketable products, local jobs and longer-term
        production capacity.
      </p>

      <div class="stat-bar">
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat-label">Plastic waste generated</p>
          <p class="stat-value">~130,000 t / year</p>
          <p class="stat-note">only around 7,200 tonnes properly recycled domestically (World Bank, 2024)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat-label">Freetown collection</p>
          <p class="stat-value">46% of households</p>
          <p class="stat-note">served by waste collection; only 25% of city waste reaches dumpsites (World Bank, 2021)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat-label">Uncollected daily</p>
          <p class="stat-value">300+ tonnes / day</p>
          <p class="stat-note">buried, burned or dumped in waterways and drains in Freetown</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Local context</p>
        <h2>Why Sierra Leone, why now</h2>
        <p>
          Sierra Leone generates an estimated 130,000 tonnes of plastic
          waste a year, while domestic recycling capacity stays far below
          national need. In Freetown, more than half of households go
          without formal waste collection, and blocked drains intensify
          flooding and public health risk. A peer-reviewed beach-litter
          study documented plastic as the dominant litter category on
          Sierra Leone's coastline, making up around 70% of litter by
          count, led by plastic bottles, water sachets, and caps and lids
          (Lavelle et al., 2024).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section panel wine" style="margin: 0 clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); width:auto; padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--blush);">Lead implementation partner</p>
    <h2>Sierra Leone Engineering Solutions</h2>
    <p style="max-width: 680px;">
      Sierra Leone Engineering Solutions (C.S.O.), led by <strong>Ishmael
      Faye</strong>, is the local implementation lead for DecoPlastic.
      The team handles operational coordination, local stakeholder
      engagement, community mobilisation and sourcing relationships on the
      ground in Sierra Leone.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">What makes DecoPlastic local</p>
        <h2>Built around Sierra Leone's own conditions</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid reveal">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="shield" />
            <h3>Aligned with national policy</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Sierra Leone has adopted a National Plastic and Plastic Waste
            Policy, and Freetown is one of five cities in UNDP and GEF's
            Shifting to Zero Waste Against Pollution (SWAP) programme.
            Sierra Leone's national SWAP component, led by the EPA and
            running 2027 to 2031, gives DecoPlastic a direct policy anchor.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="filter" />
            <h3>Careful sorting, safer production</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            A resin-based acceptance matrix guides what enters production.
            HDPE, LDPE and PP are accepted and processed, PET is kept
            separate for external recovery, and PVC, PS and mixed plastics
            are excluded for quality and safety reasons.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <Icon name="bolt" />
            <h3>Energy built for local conditions</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            Around 62% of firms in Sierra Leone own or share a generator to
            cope with frequent power outages. DecoPlastic runs on a hybrid
            solar, battery and generator system from day one, keeping
            production and equipment protected.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section panel wine" style="margin: 0 clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem) clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem); width:auto; padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); text-align:center;">
    <h2>Want to know more about DecoPlastic</h2>
    <p style="max-width:560px; margin: 0 auto 1.5em;">
      Get in touch to learn more about DecoPlastic, Sierra Leone Engineering
      Solutions, or the wider Plastic Circle West Africa programme.
    </p>
    <a class="pill-btn outline on-dark" href={`${base}contact`}>Get in Touch</a>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .pill-btn.outline.on-dark {
    border-color: var(--blush);
    color: var(--blush-pale);
  }

  .pill-btn.outline.on-dark:hover {
    background: var(--blush-pale);
    color: var(--wine-dark);
  }
</style>
